{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A desktop host does not call your HTTP route. The host starts a local Node process. Then the host writes JSON-RPC on stdin. The host reads each answer on stdout."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serveMCPStdio"},{"type":"text","value":" sends each stdin message to the server from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":". Then this function writes each answer on stdout."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"serve-on-stdio","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serve on stdio"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { serveMCPStdio } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nconst stdio = serveMCPStdio(server)\n\nconsole.error('The weather server is ready')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" from the code block."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compile "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"server.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" to JavaScript."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set the host command to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set the host arguments to the compiled file."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-stdout-for-the-protocol","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep stdout for the protocol"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stdout carries only protocol messages."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.error"},{"type":"text","value":" call in the file writes to stderr."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"console.log"},{"type":"text","value":" in this process."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The call writes on stdout. Then the host cannot parse the message."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"node-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Node only"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio"},{"type":"text","value":" entry is for Node only."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For an HTTP route, see "},{"type":"link","href":"./server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Serve tools over HTTP"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stop-the-reader","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop the reader"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"serveMCPStdio"},{"type":"text","value":" returns an object with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"close()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When stdin ends, the reader stops."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When your process must stop the reader, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stdio.close()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The host can call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get_weather"},{"type":"text","value":". The server writes the answer on stdout."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"serve-on-stdio","text":"Serve on stdio","level":2},{"id":"keep-stdout-for-the-protocol","text":"Keep stdout for the protocol","level":2},{"id":"node-only","text":"Node only","level":2},{"id":"stop-the-reader","text":"Stop the reader","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA desktop host does not call your HTTP route. The host starts a local Node process. Then the host writes JSON-RPC on stdin. The host reads each answer on stdout.\n\n`serveMCPStdio` sends each stdin message to the server from `createMCPServer`. Then this function writes each answer on stdout.\n\n## Serve on stdio\n\n```ts\n// server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { serveMCPStdio } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nconst stdio = serveMCPStdio(server)\n\nconsole.error('The weather server is ready')\n```\n\n1. Create `server.ts` from the code block.\n2. Compile `server.ts` to JavaScript.\n3. Set the host command to `node`.\n4. Set the host arguments to the compiled file.\n\n## Keep stdout for the protocol\n\nstdout carries only protocol messages.\n\nThe `console.error` call in the file writes to stderr.\n\nDo not call `console.log` in this process.\n\nThe call writes on stdout. Then the host cannot parse the message.\n\n## Node only\n\nThe `@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio` entry is for Node only.\n\nFor an HTTP route, see [Serve tools over HTTP](./server).\n\n## Stop the reader\n\n`serveMCPStdio` returns an object with `close()`.\n\nWhen stdin ends, the reader stops.\n\nWhen your process must stop the reader, call `stdio.close()`.\n\nThe host can call `get_weather`. The server writes the answer on stdout.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: MCP Server on stdio\nid: mcp-server-stdio\norder: 13\ndescription: \"Serve the same MCP server on stdin and stdout with serveMCPStdio so a desktop host can start it.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - mcp server\n  - stdio\n  - serveMCPStdio\n  - createMCPServer\n  - node\n---\n\nA desktop host does not call your HTTP route. The host starts a local Node process. Then the host writes JSON-RPC on stdin. The host reads each answer on stdout.\n\n`serveMCPStdio` sends each stdin message to the server from `createMCPServer`. Then this function writes each answer on stdout.\n\n## Serve on stdio\n\n```ts\n// server.ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\nimport { serveMCPStdio } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst getWeather = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'get_weather',\n  description: 'Get the weather for a city',\n  inputSchema: z.object({\n    city: z.string(),\n  }),\n}).server(async ({ city }) => {\n  return `Sunny in ${city}`\n})\n\nconst server = createMCPServer({\n  name: 'weather',\n  version: '1.0.0',\n  tools: [getWeather],\n})\n\nconst stdio = serveMCPStdio(server)\n\nconsole.error('The weather server is ready')\n```\n\n1. Create `server.ts` from the code block.\n2. Compile `server.ts` to JavaScript.\n3. Set the host command to `node`.\n4. Set the host arguments to the compiled file.\n\n## Keep stdout for the protocol\n\nstdout carries only protocol messages.\n\nThe `console.error` call in the file writes to stderr.\n\nDo not call `console.log` in this process.\n\nThe call writes on stdout. Then the host cannot parse the message.\n\n## Node only\n\nThe `@tanstack/ai-mcp/server/stdio` entry is for Node only.\n\nFor an HTTP route, see [Serve tools over HTTP](./server).\n\n## Stop the reader\n\n`serveMCPStdio` returns an object with `close()`.\n\nWhen stdin ends, the reader stops.\n\nWhen your process must stop the reader, call `stdio.close()`.\n\nThe host can call `get_weather`. The server writes the answer on stdout.\n"}
